<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40410" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιούσιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		either, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sufficient for the
				coming</i> (and so <i>current</i>) <i>day</i>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιοῦσα</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέρα</span>)), or, <i>for the day</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ τὴν οὖσαν</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέραν</span>)), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρτος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
					6.11
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				11.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐ</span>. dub. sens. (cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Phil.Woch.</u>
				47.889
			</span></i>) in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				5224.20
			</span></i>. (Very rare word in Origen's day, <i>De Orat.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				27.7
			</span></i>.)</div>
